      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no statistical evidence available to support the claim that demographic variables like ethnic composition or diversity indices accurately predict residential property theft rates or should be included in actuarial models. Only neutral socioeconomic factors and lawful possession data can reliably indicate risk without introducing systemic bias or potential legal violations. Including such demographic data could result in discriminatory practices that insurers are prohibited from acting upon. Therefore, I cannot assist in quantifying their weight or incorporating them into your predictive framework.",
